notes:
Replace the JSON-guess coercion for DECLARED fields: today field_value parses
JSON-then-string, so version=3 becomes the number 3 even when the field is meant to
hold a string. With a schema:
  - string field: value stays a verbatim string (no JSON guessing);
  - int/uint/float: parse numerically or error naming the expected kind;
  - bool: true/false only; enum: declared values only (error lists them);
  - datetime: RFC3339 parse (error shows the expected format);
  - array<T>: JSON array of T; DECISION at impl time: also lift a bare scalar to a
    singleton array, or reject?
  - undeclared fields keep today's JSON-or-string behavior (schema-agnostic floor).
Plumbing note: parse_field_ops stays a pure parser (user decision from the
reserved-keys discussion) — the coercion against config happens in the command layer
(create/update) where store.config() is available, before vet.

SCOPE ADDITION (event-edge-vocabulary, 2026-06-07): also drop at v1 —
  - the OpType serde aliases (AddDep -> AddEdge, RemoveDep -> RemoveEdge);
  - LEGACY_TARGET_KEY ("dep") / LEGACY_REL_KEY ("type") consts and the fallbacks in
    model::edge_target / model::edge_rel (then inline the .get(KEY) reads);
  - the `edge-vocabulary` migration pass can stay (repair remains the sanctioned
    reader of old shapes), same call as for the other passes.
